  "narrative": {
    "intro": "AmerisourceBergen Drug obligated $5B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. AmerisourceBergen Drug won 320,232 awards with an average award size of $15.7K, and obligations are down 32.5% year over year. Obligations by fiscal year show growth through FY25, with $2.1B in FY21, $2B in FY22, $4.4B in FY23, $6.1B in FY24, and $7.4B in FY25, before the current-year total of $5B. The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $5B. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the Department of Justice are distant buyers, obligating $639K and $28K respectively. Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing is the largest market for AmerisourceBergen Drug federal work at $3.4B, followed by Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers at $1.6B and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $639K. The note on account-level reporting clarifies that all figures are contract obligations except where award-value figures appear in largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are AmerisourceBergen Drug's top federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $5B with AmerisourceBergen Drug, making DoD the dominant buyer. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $639K and the Department of Justice obligated $28K. These three agencies are the top buyers listed for FY2026 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where do AmerisourceBergen Drug's federal dollars go by market?",
        "body": "Medicinal and Botanical Manufacturing received $3.4B in obligations from AmerisourceBergen Drug, the largest market. Drugs and Druggists' Sundries Merchant Wholesalers received $1.6B, and Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing received $639K. These three NAICS markets account for the major share of the vendor's FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
